avigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Senior HR Business Partner - INTERNAL ONLY Job id: 159967. Salary: £65,091 - £74,613 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance. Posted: 12 October 2026. Closing date: 18 October 2026. Business unit: Human Resources. Department: HR Business Partnering. Contact details: Ruth Watson.  Ruth.watson@kcl.ac.uk Location: Lavington Street. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search THIS VACANCY IS OPEN TO INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY About us: King’s College London is a globally leading university based across five campuses in central and southeast London. With over 40,000 students, over 12,000 employees, our mission is to make the world a better place. Our central directorates play a core role in delivering that mission, supporting our world-class research and education, and ensuring we remain in service to society. As a key member of the business partnering function, this role offers an exciting opportunity to provide HR leadership, supporting senior leaders shape and achieve their strategic aims through their teams. About the role: The HR Business Partnering teams at King’s College provide professional support and advice to more than 11,000 colleagues across the university, on the full lifecycle of employment, from recruitment and retention to reward, recognition and career development. We are proud to work with the university community to provide academic and professional excellence and an outstanding educational experience for our students. We are a people-focused team and we seek to treat colleagues fairly to bring out and reward their best. Senior HRBP’s are the front face of HR, responsible for working with the Directorates and Faculties to align our vision and our people. Working with a dedicated client group you will act as a trusted and credible partner, providing strategic advice, support and guidance on a full range of people matters. Through an understanding of the business aims and strategic priorities of your client group you will work with senior stakeholders to identify people priorities, shape solutions to their people challenges and drive forward positive change. Using your expertise and knowledge of best practice, you will challenge stakeholders to think more broadly and deeply about people matters. You will manage a small team and work with colleagues across the HR directorate, drawing on specialist expertise as needed, in the development of local initiatives and will bring business challenges and priorities back to the HR directorate to help shape the development of central initiatives and policies. This role is currently aligned to leading HR for the Estates and Facilities function, a large directorate of over 1000 staff, based in campuses across London. This is a full time time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an indefinite contract. About you: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Significant HR generalist experience within a complex, ambiguous and unionised environment, with proven success in delivering impactful strategic HR initiatives Strong coaching, facilitating and negotiating skills, with experience of working in partnership with senior stakeholders Significant experience of leading and managing organisational change Strong knowledge of employment law and HR best practice, alongside commercial and financial understanding, to enable demonstrable business focussed advice and decision making Experience of leading and managing ER casework, both formally and informally Ability to analyse complex data, identify trends and use findings to inform people strategy and initiatives Evidenced ability to develop, manage and coach team members Experience of supporting the development of strategic workforce plans Desirable criteria Experience of leading the HR aspects of large, corporate projects. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further information: At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit ’ pages. THIS VACANCY IS OPEN TO INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Senior HR Business Partner - INTERNAL ONLY | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/159967-senior-hr-business-partner-internal-only Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
