lections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160126 . Salary: £45,031 - £52,514 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 12 October 2026 . Closing date: 01 November 2026 . Business unit: Research Platforms . Department: Research Platforms Office . Contact details: Steven Lynham . Steven.lynham@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search About us King’s Smart Trials Hub (STH) is a globally distinctive multi-omics centre, located at Guy’s Hospital Campus within Research Infrastructure, part of Research Management and Innovation Directorate at King’s College London. The Hub brings together state-of-the-art spatial and non-spatial ‘omics’ technologies to enable full molecular profiling of cells, tissues and liquid biopsies and leverages advanced, multi-modal technologies to investigate disease biology at high resolution, supporting the equitable development of personalised therapies. About the role We are looking for a Technical Histology Specialist to join our collaborative and multidisciplinary team. This is an exciting opportunity to lead the delivery of specialist histology services that support innovative spatial multi-omic research. The role leads on all aspects of histological sample preparation for spatial multi-omic analysis  including processing, embedding, sectioning, mounting, staining and imaging tissues. Working closely with researchers and technical colleagues, y ou will ensure the delivery of a high-quality, customer-focused service, maintaining the highest standards of sample integrity, technical excellence and regulatory compliance. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered an ​indefinite​ contract. This is an onsite, facility-based role and the post holder is expected to be on campus for the full working week. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria 1.      PhD qualified in relevant subject area, or equivalent experience gained in a research setting. 2.      Demonstrable hands-on histology experience with sample preparation and staining techniques. 3.      Experience in microscopy and other imaging modalities, including the acquisition, analysis and interpretation of imaging data. 4.      Experience of working to quality assurance and quality control standards within a laboratory or research environment, demonstrating a high level of accuracy and attention to detail to ensure data integrity and reproducibility across workflows. 5.      Demonstrable technical problem-solving skills, with experience maintaining and troubleshooting laboratory equipment and optimising workflows to ensure high-quality and reliable research outputs. 6.      Excellent written, verbal and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate complex technical and scientific information clearly and effectively to a range of audiences through reports, publications and presentations. 7.      Demonstrable ability to work independently, prioritise competing demands, and manage multiple projects or activities simultaneously while meeting deadlines. 8.      Experience of training, mentoring or supporting others in histological techniques and laboratory procedures. Desirable criteria 1.      Practical experience with automated preparation systems such as sample processors, embedding systems and staining equipment 2.      Practical experience working with high-content slide scanners and data Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a 