Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160566 . Salary: £34,713 - £36,361 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 16 October 2026 . Closing date: 26 October 2026 . Business unit: Human Resources . Department: Executive Search . Contact details: Robyn Eade . Robyn.eade@kcl.ac.uk Location: Lavington Street . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search About us: King’s Search is King’s College London’s in-house executive search team, supporting the appointment of senior academic and professional services leaders across the university. In addition, we support special recruitment initiatives and campaigns that span multiple career level hiring. We combine executive search and recruitment expertise, in-depth knowledge of King’s and a relationship-led approach to identify and attract high-calibre talent from across the UK and internationally. Our work spans the full search or recruitment process, from market research and stakeholder engagement through to candidate management, selection and appointment. We are a specialist, collaborative team, committed to delivering a high-quality, inclusive and professional service. We use robust research methodologies, industry-standard tools and a strong understanding of the university’s priorities, faculties and professional services to support effective recruitment. Since our establishment in 2017, we have supported appointments across all nine academic faculties and a wide range of professional services, from research professors to members of the university’s senior leadership team. About the role: We are looking for a Recruitment Coordinator to join our team on a fixed-term basis, supporting the team and King’s Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine with recruitment for an exciting newly establishing research team, whose aims are to deliver innovative solutions for patients in critical care. The postholder will provide a high-quality, end-to-end recruitment service for this piece of recruitment, working within a team to support the Hiring Manager to recruit high-quality individuals across Academic, Research and Professional Services roles. The role holder will provide dedicated recruitment support, advice, and handle process administration, working closely with the project team to understand their requirements and provide pragmatic, responsive and customer-focused support throughout the recruitment process. This will include supporting recruitment activity from candidate identification through to reviewing and filtering applications, fielding enquiries and expressions of interest, coordinating interviews, downloading and collating paperwork including applications, and supporting appointment processes. The role holder will ensure that recruitment activity is delivered effectively and that candidates receive a positive and professional experience throughout. The role will also involve undertaking appropriate market research and talent identification to support recruitment activity, maintaining accurate candidate information on our database (Invenias) and engaging with prospective candidates where appropriate. The role holder will develop a broad understanding of the relevant academic disciplines, Professional Services and NHS partners, enabling them to provide informed support to stakeholders, respond confidently to candidate interest and contribute to effective talent attraction. As part of a small, collaborative in-house team, the role holder will contribute to the smooth delivery of assignments, including administration, coordination and logistics, and will work flexibly with colleagues across King’s Search. They will represent King’s College London professionally and consistently provide a high standard of service to the Hiring Manager, candidates and other stakeholders. This is a full-time post (35 hours per week), and you will be offered a fixed term contract for 6 – 8 months from joining (exact length subject to campaign requirements). About you: To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Ability to manage multiple competing priorities simultaneously. Delivery focused, with resilience and adaptability in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work closely and collaboratively in a matrix management team structure to deliver assignment outcomes. Providing supportive direction to colleagues. Able to work flexibly, a self-starter; possess sound judgement to solve day-to-day issues/challenges logically and practically before escalating issues. Excellent research and analytical skills with the ability to identify and engage talent, demonstrating excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience working within a professional setting and office environment, within a team.  Ability to coordinate diaries, update stakeholders accurately and in a timely fashion, and have proficient use of MS Teams and Outlook. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to collate information, produce high quality documentation to present to key stakeholders, whilst evidencing a commitment to professional discretion and sound judgement when handling confidential information. Experience using systems and databases to collate, store, and extract information. Desirable criteria Educated to degree level or equivalent Experience working within either a high-volume external or internal recruitment team, or an executive search function with working knowledge on the full end to end recruitment lifecycle – planning, sourcing, screening, selecting, and securing. Have a good understanding of the requirements of GDPR compliance. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further information: At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Interviews are due to be held in early November. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link"
    },
