      "title": "Senior Research Culture, Equality, Diversity & Inclusion Officer",
      "description": "Senior Research Culture, Equality, Diversity & Inclusion Officer - 0.5 FTE - INTERNAL ONLY | King's College London Skip to main content Study Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Study Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Undergraduate Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate taught Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate Research Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional Education Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Education & Languages Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Study Abroad Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Foundation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Summer and Winter Programmes Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Accommodation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Mobility Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Visit King's Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding opportunities Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Student Services Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Academic Calendar Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Sport Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Libraries & Collections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Senior Research Culture, Equality, Diversity & Inclusion Officer - 0.5 FTE - INTERNAL ONLY Job id: 160505. Salary: £42,819 per annum pro rata inclusive of London Weighting Allowance (pro -rata). Posted: 14 October 2026. Closing date: 19 October 2026. Business unit: Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine. Department: Community & Health Systems Science. Contact details: Prof Seeromanie Harding.  seeromanie.harding@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus. Category: Professional & Support Services. Back to job search THIS VACANCY IS ONLY OPEN TO INTERNAL CANDIDATES About Us The Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine (FoLSM) is one of the UK’s largest and most successful centres for biomedical research and education, ranked 9th globally in the QS World University Rankings 2026. We bring together internationally leading strengths in basic, translational and clinical science, advancing human health through world‑class research and education that benefit communities locally, nationally and globally. Our work focuses on prevention, prediction, diagnosis and management of health conditions, with growing emphasis on experimental medicine, advanced therapies, digital health and AI. Collaboration is central to our mission, with interdisciplinary teams working across the Faculty to maximise collective expertise. FoLSM employs more than 2,000 staff across six Schools and the cross‑cutting Centre for Education. We are committed to building an equitable, inclusive and diverse community, hold a Silver Athena Swan award and contribute to equality programmes across King’s. Based across four campuses (Guy’s, St Thomas’, Waterloo and Denmark Hill) we work closely with our NHS Hospital Trust partners under the King’s Health Partners Umbrella. Our 8,500 students study programmes spanning Medicine, Pharmacy, Nutrition & Dietetics, Physiotherapy and biomedical sciences. Our research excellence is reflected in REF2021, where 94.1% of submissions were rated world‑leading or internationally excellent. Our research is supported by strong national and international partnerships, including with the Francis Crick Institute. School of Life Course & Population Health Sciences ​​The  School of Life Course & Population Sciences is one of six Schools that make up the Faculty of Life Sciences & Medicine at King’s College London. The School unites over 500 experts in a wide range of population health sciences including women and children’s health, life course sciences, nutritional sciences, Health AI, preventive medicine and the molecular genetics of human disease. Our research links the causes of common health problems to life’s landmark stages, treating life, disease and healthcare as a continuum. We are interdisciplinary by nature and this innovative approach works: 91 per cent of our research submitted to the Subjects Allied to Medicine (Pharmacy, Nutritional Sciences and Women's Health cluster) for REF was rated as world-leading or internationally excellent. We use this expertise to teach the next generation of health professionals and research scientists. Based across King’s Denmark Hill, Guy’s, St Thomas’s and Waterloo campuses, our academic programme of teaching, research and clinical practice is embedded across eight Departments. About The Role We are seeking an enthusiastic and experienced individual to join the Medical Research Council Centre of Research Excellence (MRC CoRE) in Human Neural Development as Senior Research Culture, Equality, Diversity & Inclusion (CEDI) Officerr. The Centre brings together researchers, clinicians, patients and families across three world-leading universities: King’s College London, University College London and The University of Manchester. Funded for 14 years, the Centre will investigate the neurobiological principles governing human brain maturation during early development. Research Culture, Equality, Diversity and Inclusion is central to the Centre’s mission, supported by a dedicated CEDI Lead and a dynamic action plan, to ensure that the Centre is inclusive, equitable and responsive to the communities it serves. The post holder will coordinate the delivery, monitoring and evaluation of the Centre's Research Culture and CEDI action plan across this multi-site programme. Working closely with the CEDI Lead, Centre leadership, workstream leads, professional services colleagues and public contributors, they will help turn strategic commitments into practical, measurable and evidence-informed activity. A central part of the role will be to support implementation of the action plan. This will include coordinating activities across the three universities, supporting panels and working groups, developing delivery trackers, maintaining evidence sources, collecting and summarising data, and contributing to evaluation of reach, adoption, feasibility, implementation and impact. The post holder will help ensure that Centre activities are inclusive, accessible and aligned with the Equality Act 2010, and that equity considerations are embedded in recruitment, development, training, communications, public involvement and reporting. The role requires strong organisational and communication skills, confidence working with diverse stakeholders, and the ability to use qualitative and quantitative information to support learning and improvement. It will suit someone with experience in research culture, equality, diversity and inclusion, public involvement, implementation, evaluation or complex programme coordination. The post will be based in the Department of Community & Health Systems Science in the Faculty of Life Sciences and Medicine and will be line managed by Professor Seeromanie Harding. The Department has substantial expertise in the implementation and evaluation of complex systems interventions locally and internationally, with a strong emphasis on equity and improving access to development opportunities across academic and professional-services staff. It is also the academic home of Professor Emily Williams, Vice Dean (People & Culture) and Professor of Diversity, Development and Inclusion, providing access to wider expertise and research-culture initiatives across  King’s and the university sector. This is a part time post (17.5 hours per week), and you will be offered an a fixed term contract until 30 September 2033. About You To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria MSc in health-related discipline. Clear understanding of research culture, CEDI, equity principles and inclusive practices Experience in supporting the implementation and evaluation of complex interventions, and familiarity with applying implementation and evaluation  frameworks (e.g., RE-AIM, PRISM, Proctor outcomes) Demonstrable skills in qualitative methods for implementation and evaluation of complex interventions. Excellent communication, coordination, organisational and time-management skills, with the ability to work effectively across multidisciplinary teams, stakeholders and public groups while managing competing priorities and deadlines Excellent data management skills, including the ability to record, extract, analyse, interpret and present data to support equity-focused, evidence-based decision-making. Experience managing or coordinating Lived Experience, public involvement or advisory panels in an equitable way, across different sites/institutions Relevant publications, reports or outputs in implementation & evaluation, equity, CEDI or research culture. Desirable criteria Experience creating accessible and inclusive communications materials in a variety of formats for different audiences. A proactive, solutions-focused approach, with ability to work independently using sound professional judgement, contribute effectively as part of a team and support evidence-informed continuous improvement. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Senior Research Culture, Equality, Diversity & Inclusion Officer - 0.5 FTE - INTERNAL ONLY | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160505-senior-research-culture-equality-diversity-and-inclusion-officer-05-fte-internal-only Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
