o return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Portfolio Manager (Professional Education) - INTERNAL ONLY Job id: 160867 . Salary: £53,947 - £63,350 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 19 October 2026 . Closing date: 02 November 2026 . Business unit: King's Professional & Executive Dev . Department: King's Professional & Executive Dev . Contact details: Mike Bennett . mike.bennett@kcl.ac.uk Location: Strand Campus . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search THIS VACANCY IS OPEN TO INTERNAL APPLICANTS ONLY About us King’s Professional & Executive Development (KPED) is a central directorate and business owner of Professional Education at King’s.  KPED work with King’s faculties to deliver Professional Education to a wide international and domestic audience, partnering to design, develop and deliver open and bespoke educational programmes in line with King’s Vision. Our multimodal programmes include Continuing Professional Development, Executive Education, post-experience degrees and micro-credentials.  We are a small, high-powered team in an exciting area of growth and development for King’s College London.  Our portfolio is growing rapidly and expanding to include opportunities afforded through public tender, international consultancy, and market foresight. About the role This post provides a rare opportunity to play a critical role in the expansion of the professional education portfolio at King’s. As an experienced project manager, you will lead the planning and implementation of high-profile strategic workstreams, with the aim of growing the open professional education portfolio.  Working across our nine faculties, you will liaise with internal teams and external partners to develop strong commercial proposals, demonstrating excellent judgement and influence. You will work independently and proactively, while collaborating closely with the Programme Manager and the Operations team, representing King’s Professional & Executive Development (KPED) with integrity, building trust across the University and beyond. To meet this challenge, we are looking for a qualified project manager who shares our commitment to lifelong learning and widening access to a King’s education.  You will be solutions-focused and an exceptional communicator, who is able to further enhance the reputation of KPED with key stakeholders. This is a full time post, and you will be offered a fixed term contract until 30 September 2027. The role may also be considered as a secondment opportunity for internal candidates, subject to agreement with the substantive post holder's department. Key responsibilities: Oversee the end-to-end portfolio development of new professional education programmes, micro-credentials and non-credit bearing short courses, working with faculties to identify opportunities, develop business cases and progress proposals, including collaborations with external partners. Manage significant projects or workstreams to improve the learner experience and enable professional education at scale, including the development of the short course learning platform and associated digital learner journeys. Ensure that new professional programmes and micro-credentials are developed and implemented in accordance with King’s academic regulations, policies, quality assurance requirements and approval processes. Manage the approval journey for the professional education portfolio, coordinating with internal teams, and providing regular tracking reports to senior stakeholders. Develop and present data-led proposals for faculties to establish new professional education programmes and short courses. Work in close partnership with the Programme Manager (Professional Education), ensuring the operational and student-facing processes are effectively organised. Develop and enhance relationships with internal and external stakeholders for the purpose of expanding the professional education portfolio. Organise and chair relevant workstream/ project meetings. Develop and present relevant reports, recommendations and guidance for academic and professional services teams through the Professional Education Portfolio Sub-Committee, supporting effective portfolio governance and decision-making. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Undergraduate degree (or equivalent) Project management qualification Proven experience of managing project lifecycle Proven analytical and problem-solving capability Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Excellent presentation skills Proven commercial awareness in higher education Proven ability to work independently and proactively Desirable criteria Knowledge of academic programme/ course approval processes Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Interviews are due to be held on 9th or 10th November 2026 Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Portfolio Manager (Professional Education) - INTERNAL ONLY | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160867-portfolio-manager-professional-education-internal-only Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
