o return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni Open search input Jobs at King’s College London Your career Navigation link How we recruit Navigation link Our benefits Navigation link Our culture Navigation link About King's Navigation link Research Compliance Officer (Due Diligence) Job id: 160506 . Salary: £45,031 - £52,514 per annum, including London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 20 October 2026 . Closing date: 10 November 2026 . Business unit: Research Management & Innovation . Department: Research Governance, Ethics & Integrity . Contact details: Sarah Gagg . Sarah.gagg@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search About us Research and innovation are at the heart of King’s College London’s mission to make a positive difference in the world. The Research Management & Innovation Directorate (RMID) leads this ambition by shaping and enabling the university’s research and innovation agenda and creating an environment in which researchers, professional staff and doctoral students can excel. This work is guided by King’s Strategy 2030, which emphasises academic excellence, real-world impact and a culture in which research and innovation can thrive. The Department of Research Governance, Ethics and Integrity (RGEI) supports safe, ethical, lawful and responsible research across King’s. Its new Research Security team brings together work on research security, Trusted Research, compliance, due diligence and international regulatory requirements. The team develops proportionate, risk-based processes, guidance and support that help researchers manage regulatory and reputational risks while enabling valuable research and global collaboration About the role As Research Compliance Officer (Due Diligence), you will support the delivery of King’s research due diligence and compliance activities. Acting as a central point for enquiries, you will triage and coordinate requests relating to third party organisations and research collaborations, gather and validate information, undertake background checks and maintain accurate records and audit trails. You will help ensure that reviews progress efficiently, consistently and in line with institutional procedures and funder requirements. You will coordinate the University’s response to NHS R&D governance audit findings raised by NHS Trust King’s Health Partners. This will include logging and communicating findings, maintaining action plans, monitoring progress and escalating issues where required. More broadly, you will also support coordination of external funder research audits and assurance reviews, and help improve the processes, systems, guidance and reporting used to support their effective delivery. Working closely with the Research Security & Compliance Manager and colleagues across the new Research Security team, you will support the delivery of the University’s work under the UK Trusted Research framework, alongside wider research compliance activity. You will provide clear guidance to researchers and professional services colleagues, build effective relationships across teams including Procurement, Contracts, Finance and other research support teams, and escalate complex or high-risk matters to the appropriate specialist. This is a varied role requiring strong organisation, analysis and communication, together with sound judgement and close attention to detail. You will be expected to manage competing priorities, handle sensitive information appropriately and contribute to proportionate, efficient and researcher-focused compliance support. This full-time position (35 hours per week) is based at Lavington Street when campus working is required and follows the University’s hybrid working model. About you To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria 1.       Experience of working in a compliance, due dilligence, audit support, risk management or related role within a higher education institution or other complex organisation. 2.       Experience of coordinating complex administrative, compliance or assurance processes and maintaining accurate records, databases and audit trails. 3.       Experience of applying policies, procedures and regulatory requirements consistently to support decision-making and compliance activities. 4.       Strong analytical skills, with the ability to collate, assess and present information clearly to support decision-making and reporting. 5.       A high level of accuracy and attention to detail where data quality, record keeping and audit evidence are critical. 6.       Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to provide clear guidance and build effective relationships with a wide range of stakeholders. 7.       Experience of supporting reporting, monitoring, audit, assurance or review activities, including coordinating actions and tracking progress against agreed deadlines. 8.       Experience of supporting compliance, governance, assurance or risk management using a proportionate and risk-based approach. Desirable criteria 1.       Experience of working in a higher education, research or research support environment. 2.       Experience of supporting research compliance, due diligence, research assurance, research management or related activities. 3.       Experience using research management, compliance or assurance systems such as Worktribe or similar. 4.       Knowledge of the UK Trusted Research agenda, research security principles, funder compliance requirements or related regulatory frameworks. 5.       Experience of supporting responses to audits, compliance reviews, funder assurance activities or improvement programmes arising from audit or review findings. Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document provided at the bottom of the page. This document also explains which criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Apply now Apply now How we recruit At King’s we seek to recruit and retain skilled and engaged colleagues to deliver the competitive advantage. King’s benefits Our pay and benefits package attracts the best candidates from around the world. Creating meaningful impact Addressing urgent global challenges to shape a better world. Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link This website uses cookies to enhance user experience and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our site with our social media, advertising and analytics partners. Do Not Sell My Personal Information Accept Cookies Share this link on Facebook Share this link on X Share this link on Linkedin Print Email More sharing options Share content on your favourite social media platforms Close pop-up box Research Compliance Officer (Due Diligence) | King's College London https://www.kcl.ac.uk/jobs/160506-research-compliance-officer-due-diligence Share this link on Facebook Facebook Share this link on X X Share this link on Linkedin Linkedin Share this link on Pinterest Pinterest Share this link on Tumblr Tumblr Share this link on Xing Xing Share this link on Reddit Reddit Share this link on VK VK Print Print Email Email"
