. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 160985 . Salary: £34,713 - £38,127 per annum, pro rata including London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 19 October 2026 . Closing date: 02 November 2026 . Business unit: Research Management & Innovation . Department: Post Award . Contact details: Joanna Murphy . Joanna.murphy@kcl.ac.uk Location: Guy's Campus . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search About us: The Research Grants & Contracts team within King’s College London supports the successful delivery of one of the UK's largest and most diverse research portfolios. Our Post-Award service works with researchers, faculties and professional services colleagues to ensure research funding is managed effectively throughout its lifecycle. As part of an exciting programme of service development, we are strengthening our support at key points in the research award lifecycle, helping research projects move efficiently from award acceptance to project activation, delivery and closure. This role sits within our Post-Award team and will play an important part in improving project setup performance, reducing delays and supporting excellent service for our research community. The role contributes to a wider ambition to move towards a more proactive, risk-based approach to research award management and service improvement About the role: We are looking for a highly organised and proactive individual to join our Post-Award team as a Research Grants Project Setup Coordinator. This is a varied coordination and administration role focused on the project setup phase of the research award lifecycle. You will help ensure new research awards are activated accurately and efficiently by coordinating information, monitoring progress, maintaining records and working with colleagues across faculties and professional services teams to resolve routine issues that may delay project activation. You will become a key point of contact for project setup activity, helping to track awards through the setup process, support risk assessment activities, maintain accurate data and produce management information. Working closely with Research Grants Managers, Research Grants Administrators and colleagues across King’s, you will help ensure research projects can start promptly and in compliance with funder and university requirements. The role offers an excellent opportunity to develop broad knowledge of research funding and university research administration. We welcome applications from individuals looking to build a career in research management, those seeking to expand existing research administration experience, or experienced professionals looking for a flexible part-time opportunity. This is a part time post (17.5 per week), and you will be offered an indefinite contract. This will be operating on a ‘hybrid working’ basis with a minimum of one day a week in the office. About you: To be successful in this role, you will be highly organised, detail-oriented and enjoy coordinating activity across multiple stakeholders and priorities. You will be someone who takes pride in maintaining accurate information, following processes and helping others navigate administrative procedures. Essential criteria Experience of providing high-quality administrative support within a busy operational environment, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities simultaneously. Excellent organisational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to maintain accurate records, monitor progress and ensure work is completed within agreed timescales. Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build effective working relationships and communicate clearly with a wide range of stakeholders. Ability to work effectively within established procedures, identify issues or inconsistencies, and escalate matters appropriately when required. Good numeracy skills and confidence working with data and information. Experience of using digital systems and Microsoft Office applications to maintain information, produce reports and support administrative processes. Ability to work collaboratively as part of a team, demonstrating flexibility and a willingness to support colleagues during periods of increased workload or absence. Desirable criteria Experience of working within a higher education, research administration, finance, compliance or other professional services environment. Knowledge of research funding administration or the research award lifecycle gained through work experience, study or professional development. Experience of Worktribe research management tool and Unit 4 Business World (King’s finance system). Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here . We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘How we Recruit’ pages. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation link Alumni Footer navigation link Facilities Student services Footer navigation link Accommodation Footer navigation link Libraries & Collections Footer navigation link King’s IT Footer navigation link Academic Calendar Footer navigation link Discover King's News Centre Footer navigation link Events Footer navigation link Student's Union Footer navigation link Visit King's Footer navigation link Work at King's Footer navigation link King's community Footer navigation link Contact us +44 (0)20 7836 5454 King's College London Strand London WC2R 2LS United Kingdom Terms & conditions Footer navigation link Privacy policy Footer navigation link Modern slavery statement Footer navigation link Site help Footer navigation link Accessibility Footer navigation link Manage cookies Footer navigation link"
