      "title": "Senior Director of Professional Services Integration",
      "description": "Senior Director of Professional Services Integration - INTERNAL ONLY | King's College London Skip to main content Opens navigation menu Study Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Study Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Undergraduate Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate taught Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Postgraduate Research Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional Education Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Education & Languages Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Study Abroad Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu International Foundation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Summer and Winter Programmes Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Accommodation Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Mobility Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Visit King's Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding opportunities Navigation link in category Study. Press escape key to return to main menu Student Services Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Student Services Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Academic Calendar Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Sport Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Libraries & Collections Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student's Union Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Careers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Language Centre Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s IT Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Answers Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Mental health and wellbeing Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Student news Navigation link in category Student Services. Press escape key to return to main menu Research & Innovation Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Research & Innovation Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Explore Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Impact Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Research Environment Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Funding Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Facilities Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Collaborate with King's Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Health Partners Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Doctoral College Navigation link in category Research & Innovation. Press escape key to return to main menu Our faculties Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. Our faculties Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Arts & Humanities Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Law Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Nursing, Midwifery & Palliative Care Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Business Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Life Sciences & Medicine Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Psychiatry, Psychology & Neuroscience Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Natural, Mathematical & Engineering Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Dentistry, Oral & Craniofacial Sciences Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu Social Sciences & Public Policy Navigation link in category Our faculties. Press escape key to return to main menu About Navigation category. Contains links. Press enter key to expand. About Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu History Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Strategy Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Learning & Teaching Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Our People Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Work at King's Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Partnerships Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Governance, policies & procedures Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Professional & Support Services Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Diversity & Inclusion Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Financial information Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King’s Impact Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu King's Venues Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Sustainability Navigation link in category About. Press escape key to return to main menu Students Staff Alumni King's College London Job id: 161665 . Salary: £120,000 to £125,000 per annum plus London Weighting Allowance . Posted: 20 October 2026 . Closing date: 03 November 2026 . Business unit: Executive Portfolios . Department: Merger Management Office . Contact details: Jeremy Cook . Jeremy.Cook@kcl.ac.uk Location: Strand Campus . Category: Professional & Support Services . Back to job search THIS VACANCY IS OPEN TO INTERNAL CANDIDATES ONLY About The Role The Senior Director of Professional Services Integration will provide strategic leadership for the planning, coordination and delivery of the professional services integration programme for the merger between King’s College London and Cranfield University to become a £1.8Bn university and a £750-800m PS workstream. Working across all Professional Service functions and in close partnership with other parts of the Merger Management Office (MMO) and workstream leads, the postholder will lead the development and implementation of integration plans that enable the successful transition to a single University over the next 2-3 years. The role will be responsible for shaping and coordinating the professional services integration strategy for the merger, translating institutional objectives into deliverable programmes of work. The postholder will ensure alignment across functions, identify and manage critical interdependencies, mitigate operational, regulatory and organisational risks, and provide advice and assurance to support executive decision-making. They will oversee a complex portfolio of transformation activity spanning all professional service domains, including IT, Estates & Facilities, Students & Academic Services Division, RMID, Finance, Philanthropy & Alumni, Comms & Engagement, Chairman’s Office and HR. The Senior Director will report to the SVP (Operations) but be part of the MMO and will need to build a strong relationship with the Senior Director of the MMO and the Executive Director, Strategic Assurance.  They will support, advise and prepare the Joint PS Integration Steering Group, which is co-Chaired by the Chief Operating Officers of Cranfield University and King’s. The Senior Director will play the most critical role in preparing the institution for day one readiness and ensuring sustainable PS integration beyond day one, developing target integration plans and operating models across all PS functions and helping to realise the strategic benefits of the merger and deliver the ambitions of King's Strategy 2030 and beyond. This is a full-time post and you will be offered  a fixed term contract for 18 months. About You To be successful in this role, we are looking for candidates to have the following skills and experience: Essential criteria Significant senior leadership experience delivering large-scale organisational transformation, integration, restructuring or merger programmes within a complex organisation. Experience of operating successfully at executive level, providing strategic advice, challenge and assurance to senior leaders, governing bodies and executive decision-making forums. Significant experience leading complex, multi-disciplinary transformation portfolios spanning multiple functions, stakeholders and organisational boundaries. Proven ability to design and lead engagement and change management approaches that secure stakeholder buy-in, support adoption and enable successful delivery of complex organisational transformation. Proven ability to identify, assess and manage complex strategic, operational, financial, regulatory and organisational risks. Outstanding stakeholder management and influencing skills, with the ability to secure alignment across diverse groups where authority may be indirect. Exceptional strategic thinking, analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to shape institutional strategy and translate complex objectives into deliverable outcomes. Evidence of leading and developing high-performing teams through periods of significant change and organisational uncertainty. Desirable criteria Experience of merger, acquisition or institutional integration activity within higher education or another similarly complex sector. Knowledge of higher education regulatory and governance environments. Formal programme or project management qualification (MSP, PRINCE2, APM, PMP or equivalent). Downloading a copy of our Job Description Full details of the role and the skills, knowledge and experience required can be found in the Job Description document, provided at the bottom of the page. This document will provide information of what criteria will be assessed at each stage of the recruitment process. Further Information At King’s, we believe that the diversity of our community and a culture that is welcoming, open, inclusive and collaborative, are great strengths of the university. The Equality Act of 2010 protects the rights of our students and staff and provides a framework to fulfil our duties to eliminate unlawful discrimination, harassment and victimisation and in addition, to advance equality of opportunity and foster good relations between those who share a protected characteristic and those who do not. At times, this will include balancing rights and beliefs that can feel in tension. We are committed to free speech and to academic freedom, believing that our foundational purpose as a university, is to create spaces where a wide range of ideas, including ideas that are controversial, can be discussed and debated, and where members of our community can express lawful views without fear of intimidation, harassment or discrimination. When engaging in the robust exchange of ideas, we ask that our community is mindful of our Dignity at King’s guidance. We ask all candidates to submit a copy of their CV, and a supporting statement, detailing how they meet the essential criteria listed in the person specification section of the job description. If we receive a strong field of candidates, we may use the desirable criteria to choose our final shortlist, so please include your evidence against these where possible. Artificial intelligence (AI) is evolving rapidly, and we recognise its growing role in professional work. Applicants may use AI tools to support preparation of their application, for example to research the role or structure written responses. However, applications must reflect the applicant’s own work and experience. AI tools should not be used during interviews or assessment activities unless this has been agreed in advance as a reasonable adjustment. Further guidance on the use of AI in recruitment can be found here. We reserve the right to close adverts early due to the volume of applications we receive. While the closing date may change, all adverts will close at 23:59 to allow sufficient time for applications to be submitted on that day. We encourage you to apply at the earliest opportunity to avoid disappointment as once we have closed a vacancy you will be unable to submit your application. To find out how our managers will review your application, please take a look at our ‘ How we Recruit ’ pages. Apply now Apply now Connect with King’s College London Study Degree courses Footer navigation link Postgraduate taught Footer navigation link Postgraduate research Footer navigation link International Footer navigation link Summer schools Footer navigation link Student experience Footer navigation link Information for New students Footer navigation link Current students Footer navigation link Staff Footer navigation l